const EXP={"Needs attention":"Things to fix or review: missing numbers, months not reviewed yet, and tax steps not finished. Click an item to go straight to it.","Properties":"How many rentals you own (properties on Active Rentals).","Lifetime rent income":"All rent and late fees collected from every property, from the first month you entered through today.","Lifetime profit / (loss) - with acquisition cost":"Everything you collected minus everything you spent, including what you paid to buy each property (down payment, closing costs, repairs at purchase).","Lifetime profit / (loss) - without acquisition cost":"Everything you collected minus your monthly costs (mortgage, repairs, misc, insurance, taxes). Leaves out what you paid to buy the properties.","Portfolio value (purchase prices)":"The purchase prices of all your properties added up. Not today's market value.","Est. proceeds if sold (today, after tax)":"About what you would walk away with if you sold everything today: estimated value (purchase price grown by the appreciation rate), minus selling costs, loan balances and the tax on the sale (including depreciation recapture).","Lifetime avg monthly cash flow":"Your average profit per month across all months entered (rent and late fees minus all monthly costs).","Lifetime cash on cash":"Yearly cash flow divided by the cash you put in to buy (acquisition cost). Shows how hard your money is working.","Profit & Loss by year":"Each year's revenue, expenses and profit. Pick whether expenses include what you paid to buy the properties.","Year":"The calendar year.","Acquisition cost to date":"What you paid to buy the properties owned by that year: down payment, closing costs and repairs at purchase.","Total revenue":"Rent and late fees, plus tax savings where shown.","Total expenses":"All money spent: mortgage, repairs, misc, insurance and property taxes (plus acquisition cost if that option is picked).","Profit / (loss)":"Total revenue minus total expenses. A loss shows in red with a minus sign.","Cumulative profit / (loss)":"The running total of profit or loss, adding each year to the ones before it.","Cumulative profit":"The running total of profit, adding each year to the ones before it.","Total":"All rows added up.","Property":"The rental property (named after its address in Deals).","Tax type":"How the IRS treats this rental: REPS (you are a real estate professional), STR (short-term rental you work in yourself) or doesn't qualify (passive - losses can't lower your job income). Change it here or in Deals - they stay in sync.","State":"The state the property is in. Rental income is taxed by that state, and your home state gives you a credit for that tax.","Rental profit for taxes":"Rent plus late fees, minus insurance and property taxes, for the year. Mortgage principal is not a write-off, so it is not taken out here.","Write-offs":"Everything you can deduct for this property this year: depreciation, bonus depreciation (purchase year), loan interest, repairs, management, legal and other expenses, and repeat costs.","How":"Where the write-off numbers come from: your CPA, numbers you entered, or standard depreciation figured automatically.","Loan Interest":"Interest only - from the 1098 your lender sends each year. Principal is not a write-off.","Repairs, Maintenance":"Repairs you can write off this year. Big improvements are depreciated over many years instead.","Property Management & Advertising/Marketing":"Manager fees, listing and booking fees, ads and photos.","Legal, Professional Fees":"CPA, tax prep, attorney and bookkeeping fees.","Other Expenses":"Anything else you can deduct: travel to the property, supplies, software, utilities you pay.","Estimated tax savings":"How much less tax you pay this year because of your rentals, compared to owning no rentals. Shown as the middle of a low-high range.","Your tax bill (what you pay)":"Federal + state income tax + self-employment (or paycheck) tax, with your rentals included.","With no rentals (what you would have paid)":"The same tax bill figured as if you owned no rentals. The difference is your tax savings.","With no rentals":"The tax math as if you owned no rentals.","With your rentals":"The tax math with your rentals included.","Personal income after personal deductions":"Your job or business income minus your personal deductions (like retirement contributions).","Rental profit (+) or paper loss (-)":"Rental profit for taxes minus write-offs. A paper loss lowers your other income if the property qualifies (REPS or STR).","Half of self-employment tax (deductible)":"1099 and self-employed people can deduct half of their self-employment tax.","Standard deduction (single)":"The amount of income the IRS does not tax. You get the bigger of this or your itemized deductions.","Standard deduction (married filing jointly)":"The amount of income the IRS does not tax. You get the bigger of this or your itemized deductions.","QBI deduction":"Qualified business income deduction - up to 20% of business income for 1099 and S corp owners. Rental losses can shrink it.","Federal taxable income":"Income left after all deductions. Federal brackets apply to this.","Federal income tax":"Tax figured from the IRS brackets on your federal taxable income.","NC bonus depreciation adjustment":"North Carolina only allows 15% of bonus depreciation the first year. The other 85% is added back to NC income and given back over the next 5 years.","NC state income tax":"North Carolina tax at its flat rate on NC income.","Self-employment tax":"Social Security and Medicare for self-employed income (15.3% up to the wage cap). Rentals don't change it.","Total tax bill":"Federal + state + self-employment (or paycheck) tax.","Tax savings (vs. owning no rentals)":"Tax bill with no rentals minus tax bill with your rentals.","What to do":"Next steps to make your tax estimate more exact.","Month":"The month of the row.","Rent":"Rent collected for the month.","MTG Payment":"The full mortgage payment for the month (principal + interest + escrow if included).","Repairs":"Repair and maintenance money spent that month.","MISC":"Any other cost that month (utilities, supplies, fees).","Insurance":"Property insurance paid (monthly, or the yearly amount in the month you paid it).","Taxes":"Property taxes paid.","Late fees":"Late fees collected from the tenant.","Monthly income":"Rent + late fees minus all costs for that month.","Running total":"Total profit so far, minus what you paid to buy the property. When it turns positive you have made your money back.","Total Income":"All rent and late fees so far.","Total Spent":"All costs so far.","Running Net Income Without acquisition cost":"Total income minus total spent, not counting what you paid to buy the property.","Total Income (rent + late fees)":"All rent and late fees for the period.","Total tax savings":"Tax savings from this property for the period (its share of your total savings).","TOTAL REVENUE AND TAX SAVINGS":"Income plus tax savings - the full benefit of the property.","Acquisition cost":"What you paid to buy the property: down payment, closing costs (after seller credits) and repairs at purchase.","Mortgage, repairs, misc, insurance, taxes":"All monthly costs added up.","Spent deduction":"Extra money spent around the purchase that you entered separately.","TOTAL SPENT":"Acquisition cost plus all monthly costs.","P&L":"Profit and loss: total revenue and tax savings minus total spent.","Offered":"Deals you made an offer on.","Pending":"Deals under contract.","Waiting Tenant":"Bought and waiting for a tenant.","Active Tenant":"Bought with a tenant in place.","Deals":"Every property you are looking at. Fill in the numbers, then Move to active rental when you buy it.","Color":"A color tag you pick to sort deals at a glance. It also shows on the property in Active Rentals.","Address":"The property address. Paste a Zillow link to open the listing.","Price":"Asking or purchase price.","SPCC":"Seller paid closing costs - money the seller covers at closing.","Style":"Single-family, multi-family or townhouse.","HOA":"Is there a homeowners association?","HOA Fee":"The monthly HOA fee.","Cost seg study":"Will you get a cost seg study? Yes: the bonus depreciation box shows in the purchase year on Taxes, and the rest of the building is depreciated over 27.5 years (39 for short-term rentals). No: no bonus box - straight-line depreciation on the building value: 90% of the first $175,000 of the price + 83% of anything above.","Purchased":"The month you bought (or will buy) the property. Used for depreciation and the first month on Active Rentals.","Pros/Cons + Comments":"Your notes about the deal.","Input":"The numbers you type for this deal.","Value":"The dollar amount used. Calculated from the assumed % unless you type a manual amount.","Assumed %":"A percentage used when you don't type a manual amount.","Manual Input":"Type an exact dollar amount here to replace the assumed %.","Purchase Price":"What you pay for the property.","Cash purchase (no loan)":"Yes if you pay all cash. The down payment becomes 100% and there is no loan.","Down Payment":"Cash you put down. The rest is the loan.","Closing Costs":"Lender and title fees at closing. Default is 2% of the price + $5,500.","Seller Paid Closing Costs":"Closing costs the seller pays for you. They lower your cash needed.","Net Closing Costs":"Closing costs minus what the seller pays.","Interest Rate":"The yearly interest rate on the loan.","Term in years":"How many years the loan lasts.","Financed Amount":"The loan: purchase price minus down payment.","Payment":"Monthly principal and interest on the loan.","Renovations/Repairs":"Money spent fixing the property up when you buy it.","Out of Pocket Costs":"Total cash needed to buy: down payment + net closing costs + renovations.","After Repair Value":"What the property is worth after repairs. Used for equity and sale estimates.","Assumed Appreciation":"How much the property value grows each year.","Selling Costs":"Agent and closing costs when you sell, as a % of the sale price.","Monthly":"The monthly income and costs for this deal.","Property Mgmt":"Property manager fee, as a % of rent or a dollar amount.","Vacancy":"Rent lost to empty months, as a % of rent.","Maintenance/Repairs":"Money set aside for repairs, as a % of rent.","CapEx":"Money set aside for big replacements (roof, HVAC), as a % of rent.","Property Taxes":"Yearly property tax divided by 12.","Expenses Subtotal":"All monthly operating costs, not counting the mortgage.","Annual % Increase (rent + expenses)":"How much rent and costs go up each year in the projections.","Output":"The results for this deal.","Monthly Expenses":"Mortgage payment plus all monthly operating costs.","Monthly Net Cash Flow":"Rent minus monthly expenses.","Initial Cash on Cash":"First-year cash flow divided by out of pocket costs.","IRR Lifetime Average":"The yearly return over the life of the deal, counting cash flow and the sale.","Years":"Years after purchase.","Investment":"Cash you put in (out of pocket costs).","Cash Return":"Cash flow for that year.","CoC":"Cash on cash: that year's cash flow divided by your investment.","Annual Equity":"Value minus loan balance in that year.","IRR (If Sold)":"Your yearly return if you sold at the end of that year.","Total Return $ (If Sold)":"Cash you would get from the sale in that year, after selling costs and paying off the loan.","Rental income + late fees":"Projected rent and late fees.","Operating expenses":"Projected mortgage, repairs, misc, insurance and taxes.","Acquisition + spent deduction":"What you paid to buy, counted in the purchase year.","Cash flow (no tax savings)":"Revenue minus expenses, before tax savings.","Cash on cash":"Cash flow divided by the cash you put in to buy.","Total spent":"All costs for the year.","Running total spent":"All costs added up year after year.","Rental income":"Rent and late fees.","Tax savings":"Estimated tax savings from your rentals that year.","Running total revenue":"Revenue added up year after year.","Running net":"Running total revenue minus running total spent.","1. About you*":"Your income, filing status and job type for the year. Rental savings are figured against this.","2. Your write-offs*":"Each property's rental profit for taxes and write-offs for the year. Click Edit to change the write-offs.","3. Results*":"Your estimated tax savings from rentals, and the full tax math with and without your rentals.","Profit & Loss -*":"This property's money in and money out for the year.","What-if: buy another property*":"Adds a pretend property to your real numbers for this year and shows how much your tax savings change.","Projected yearly review*":"Projections for the coming years using the yearly increases in Settings.","10-year running totals*":"Running totals over 10 years for each property.","Closed deals":"Deals you moved to Active Rentals. Their numbers feed those properties - edit them here.","Repeat costs*":"Costs that happen several times a year (like cleanings). Enter the cost and how many times.","Calculated / locked":"Figured by the app from other numbers. You can't type here.","Estimate":"An estimate from the assumed percentages, not a real number yet.","Auto-filled":"Filled in for you from other numbers. You can change the assumed % or type a manual amount.","Your input":"Numbers you type in yourself."};
